 outside the lab."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"I’ve led engineering teams, field crews and equipment vendors through nationwide deployments where the spec sheet promised one thing and the site delivered another. Closing that gap before the build is how I work, and it is the same gap Physical AI faces now."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"My current work spans Physical AI, edge inference, model optimization, computer vision, runtime observability, and operational safety. Across my flagship projects, I work with Jetson-based inference, ROS 2 robotics, simulation, defensive telemetry, and time-series forecasting, with AI-RAN KPIs as one telemetry source among others."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The common thread is simple: AI systems should not just run once in a demo. They should be measurable, observable, reliable, and useful under real constraints. My passion is bridging the sim-to-real gap."}]]}]]}]]}],"$L6","$L7","$L8","$L9"]}]
